WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.230
We shall rebuild Konomi-san's body.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.230
Rebuild... my body?!

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.580
<i>Muscles won't ever betray you.</i>

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.510
<i>They will be on your side all day, every day.</i>

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:20.920
<i>They are close friends 
you can trust with your life.</i>

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.120
<i>The more you train, 
the more effort you put in,</i>

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.160
<i>the more your muscles will repay you.</i>

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:32.070
<i>When you're swole, you will be fulfilled 
both physically and mentally.</i>

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.080
<i>And when your body and mind 
reach perfect harmony,</i>

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.390
<i>your muscles will make you 
shine like never before.</i>

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:03.660
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:20.990
Fight! Fight!

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.960
You do laps for climbing, too?

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:20.990
Maybe not if you're just gym climbing, 
but competitive climbers do.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.250
Konomi-san, you couldn't send the route 
at the tournament, remember?

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:27.750
Yes.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.360
There were several reasons for that,

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.450
but the most obvious one 
was your lack of strength.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.580
That's understandable, 
considering you only just started.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.260
Our next objective is the Kanto High School 
Bouldering Championship in two months.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.020
In that time, we'll rebuild your 
body into one that can compete.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:49.740
You have the potential to aim much higher.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.520
Got it!

00:02:51.520 --> 00:03:01.660
Fight! Fight!

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.530
<b><i>Wall 3     The Anti-Monkey Rock</i></b>

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.660
If anything, you're a bit chubby, 
so you gotta lose some weight.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.660
Ch-Chubby?!

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:09.410
Losing two kilos opens up more options 
than gaining two kilos of grip strength.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:14.060
You've gotta be able to carry your weight 
all the way up with just your limbs.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.420
Chub... Chubby?

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.230
Gotcha!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.800
Hey, Nono-san!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.360
Gotta trim that fat, girl!

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.300
Chubby...

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.560
How exactly am I supposed 
to build up strength?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.630
Basically, you'll work on base strength,
 pulling and pushing power,

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.580
core strength, and the ability 
to maintain position...

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.570
Foundational muscle strength for climbers.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:43.320
Next up, incline sprints. 
We'll all go at once.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.700
<i>Chubby...</i>

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.330
Is something the matter, Konomi-san?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.580
No, nothing!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.560
Go!

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:56.120
But it'll be different from bodybuilding.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.070
You're only looking to 
gain <i>functional</i> muscle.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:03.260
Getting too jacked will 
only add excess weight.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.060
Yes! 

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.220
No! 

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.120
One-legged squats!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.970
<i>Chubby...</i>

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.480
Okay, let's do some short problems.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.170
<i>Chubby...</i>

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.020
Focus, Konomi.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.110
O-Oh, right.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.110
Nicely done, Captain.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.110
Nice, Sayo-chin.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.110
Nice, Konomi!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.400
<i>I had such a hard time 
with a short problem...</i>

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.180
Okay, now let's campus that problem.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.370
"Campus"?

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.160
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.880
<i>I sent this earlier, but now 
 my legs won't move.</i>

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.380
<i>I can't even complete one move?</i>

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.740
Climbing using your arms 
alone is called "campusing."

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.640
This trains your upper body to...

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.960
Are you okay, Konomin?!

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:57.900
Are you all right?

00:04:58.770 --> 00:04:59.640
<i>Ch...</i>

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.640
Begin hanging leg raises!

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.180
One, two, three, right.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.780
One, two, three, left.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.090
One, two, three...

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.780
Konomin down!

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:15.540
One, two, one, two...

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.790
We lost Konomin again!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.290
Konomin!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.800
My entire body hurts.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.300
Training is really hard.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.940
Huh?

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:33.900
Jun-chan.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.860
Let's eat together, okay?

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.810
I-I don't mind.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.270
Yay! Thanks!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:49.660
I see you by yourself most of the time. 
Do you prefer being alone?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.370
What? Is that a problem?!

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.500
No, no, of course not!

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:00.580
Well, you know how I am. 
I'm not great at socializing.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:05.230
I've been obsessed with climbing forever 
and don't have any other hobbies,

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.090
so I have an easier time by myself.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:09.970
I see.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.940
Konomi, you've better doing 
better in practice lately,

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.850
but you're still way off 
where you need to be.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:22.230
If you can't handle this regimen,
 you'll fail the prelims in the next event, too.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.860
So, you need to...

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:30.240
<i>I'm doing it again.</i>

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.820
<i>Being such a hardass on everyone 
is the reason I don't have any friends.</i>

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:40.680
Later.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.750
You see right through me, huh?

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:57.020
You're absolutely right. 
I'm sore all over again.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.520
But you know what?

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:04.400
I've never worked toward a 
common goal with a team before.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.600
So, while it is hard,
 I'm enjoying this new experience.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.410
I'm really happy right now!

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.150
<i>This girl...</i>

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.610
Oh, sorry for keeping you.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:16.790
It's fine.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.910
Let's eat together again, okay, Jun-chan?

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:27.530
<i>I've always thought climbing 
was all I ever wanted,</i>

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.050
<i>and that I didn't need friends...</i>

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:35.430
Are you sure you want
 me around during lunch?

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:40.330
Keep in mind, I'll be
 monitoring your calorie intake.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.280
No!

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.070
What? Having doubts about your diet?

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.440
Uh, that's not it...

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.440
Looks like I'm going to have my hands full.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.450
Oh... Cut me some slack, boss.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.200
Three more seconds.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.200
Three, two, one.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.200
Okay, let's do some cooldown 
stretches and call it a day.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.480
'Kay!

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.840
Huh? Are finishing up early today?

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:18.850
It's because we have a road trip tomorrow,
 my dear Konomi-kun.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:23.440
Oh, that's right. A practice match, right?

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.100
Who are we facing?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.550
A truly formidable opponent, that's who.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.360
It's called the Anti-Monkey Rock.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.430
The Anti-Monkey Rock?

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.110
It's just what it sounds like.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:40.370
It's a rock that even monkeys can't climb.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.000
P-Poor monkeys!

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:49.000
Huh? Nobody's here.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.000
Why?

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.270
Did I come to the wrong place?

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:55.900
"Jun-chan, where are you? 
I don't see you all."

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.600
Heck, I don't see <i>anyone,</i> for that matter.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.760
<i>Yakisoba!</i>

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:03.270
<b>Jun-chan</b>

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:03.270
<b>You're an hour early</b>

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.390
<i>You're an hour early, idiot.</i>

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.270
<b>Idiot</b>

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.820
Hello.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.660
What are you up to?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:21.760
A game.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.590
Oh, that I can tell.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.970
I was just wondering what 
you were doing here.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.620
ZWBY is fun, isn't it?

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:32.110
You can play?

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:34.550
Huh? I can, why?

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:36.330
1v1 me.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:40.110
What? I used to be pretty hardcore, you know?

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.430
It'll be fine.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:45.930
I've never met anyone better than me.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.440
I-I lost ten in a row!

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:53.690
S-Sorry. I used to be a top-tier ZWBYian...

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.320
<i>Yikes. Did I go overboard?</i>

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.700
L-L... Le...

00:09:58.700 --> 00:09:59.700
Le?

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.230
Let me call you "Master"!

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.020
Sorry, Master, my dad is calling me back.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.210
Sure, go ahead.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:17.480
I couldn't beat you even once, 
but I'm happy I met someone so good.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:18.840
Let's play again.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:19.720
Sure.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.600
See you, Master.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:24.100
Y-Yeah, see you.

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:29.160
Wait, I didn't get her contact info!

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.100
<i>Yakisoba!</i>

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.480
Uh, an hour's passed...

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.360
You show up early and you're still late?

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.490
I'm sorry!

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.990
You're not cut out for group activities.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.080
You're one to talk!

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.410
What about me?

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:53.000
You're always going off 
and doing whatever and stuff.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.880
Huh? I can't hear you.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:55.640
You're such a...

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:57.210
They seem awfully friendly now.

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:58.010
Yeah, yeah, I'm sorry!

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.460
Rocks, like climbing walls, 
have difficulty grades.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:06.170
The Anti-Monkey Rock has a V6 problem,

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:10.520
and other more difficult problems, 
going all the way to V10.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:14.020
I'm going to attempt a V8 today.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:19.310
It'll be difficult for you to fully climb it, 
since it's your first time,

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.530
but start with the V6 and see how you go.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:22.970
Okay!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.790
There's someone climbing over there!

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:40.920
Awesome.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:56.110
Wow, he actually climbed all the way.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.830
That was incredible, Juzo-san.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.010
Miss Yotsuba.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:07.710
It's nice to see you again.

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:11.000
Let me introduce you.
 This is Goto Juzo-san.

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:15.310
He's a bouldering specialist who holds 
numerous outdoor climbing records.

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.900
He coaches us every now and then.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:22.510
No, I don't. You just happen 
to be there when I'm climbing.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:25.680
Dad.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.140
Oh, Kiku-chan.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.640
Long time no see. How have you been?

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:32.390
Huh?

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:38.320
I knew it.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.280
Master!

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.640
"Master"?

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:46.090
Oh, uh, it's a long story.

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:47.280
Is it?

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:51.910
I'm amazed you know Kiku-chan, Konomi.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.920
It's more like I just 
got to know her earlier.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.600
What? Don't tell me you actually managed 
to have a conversation with her?!

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:00.920
I guess you could say that...

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:05.290
Amazing. I'd love to have 
a chat with her, too,

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:08.300
but she doesn't talk to us much.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.060
Really?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.310
What the heck?

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.220
She's such a tough nut to crack for me.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:15.500
Nonoka, the mat.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:16.310
I know.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.620
But lucky you, Konomin.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:19.720
Right...

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:21.310
Get ready, Konomi-san.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:22.320
Okay!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:29.320
<i>So, this is the Anti-Monkey Rock. 
Let's do this.</i>

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:38.330
This thing has eight routes...

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:43.200
No, if you count the ones that 
merge partway, ten routes.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.170
You can tell? You haven't 
even checked a topo guide.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.220
But they all look difficult.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.290
The only one I might be able to climb

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:54.850
is the one that turns to the 
top-right from around the middle.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:58.490
Bingo. That's the V6 problem.

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:00.110
Impressive observation, as always.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:04.940
Go for it, Konomi.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:06.620
Hang in there, Konomin!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:09.240
<i>This is real rock climbing...</i>

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.460
<i>It's nothing like the 
holds on the wall in school!</i>

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.500
<i>It's so rough!</i>

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.990
Yeah, that's the way.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.250
Keep going!

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.000
<i>Next up is that crack over there.</i>

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.570
Ouch!

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.760
<i>The crack is next...</i>

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:41.770
<i>My right hand froze!</i>

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:44.810
<i>Why won't you move, hand?</i>

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:49.430
<i>Why? I haven't even climbed all that far!</i>

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:00.140
<i>I'm scared!</i>

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:06.240
Nice landing, Konomi.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:08.220
No need to push yourself at the start.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.800
It'd be dangerous if you got too far.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.100
So, how did your first 
bouldering attempt feel?

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:20.010
Unlike walls, rock faces are 
intimidating on a primal level.

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:22.650
This is one of the reasons:

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:27.690
the high risk attached to falling in itself, 
because even that could injure you.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:33.610
In competitive bouldering, 
you can keep going even after you fall,

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:38.200
so you kinda start thinking it's 
okay to fall and take it lightly.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:42.040
Right now, you're working on 
your strength and technique,

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:45.960
but there's one more major thing 
you need to be able to win.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:52.220
It's the fortitude to keep climbing 
when you know you can't afford to fall.

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.490
Fortitude...

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:58.730
Go, Jun!

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.500
Fight, Jun-chan!

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:17.770
Amazing, Jun! You actually sent the V8!

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:18.990
Thank you!

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.870
Dad, can you spot for me?

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.750
Given where she's starting, 
is she attempting the same route as Jun?

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:33.760
No. She's traversing to the right,
 so it's the V10 problem.

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:37.760
She changed her route?

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.770
It's a mixture of both 
the V10 problems here...

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:44.020
The most difficult route this rock has.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:45.770
She's at the crux!

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:50.940
At the end of a long sequence of moves that 
drain you, you have to execute a mantel

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.050
which is very demanding and even scarier.

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:58.280
Incredible. And she's still 
only in junior high school, too.

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:00.180
Wow.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:04.740
She's probably the best girl boulderer
 in junior high, period.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.790
That was amazing, Kiku-chan!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:11.550
You can climb such a difficult route!

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:17.580
Well, I've been climbing this rock for years.

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:20.090
I actually think your eyes are more amazing.

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:21.180
Really?

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.160
Yeah.

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:26.490
Unlike walls, rock faces 
don't have routes marked out,

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.610
so they require even more analytic skill.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:33.940
You figured out all the routes on sight. 
That's an amazing ability.

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:36.860
I was right to call you my master.

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:42.160
Th-Thanks, Kiku-chan.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:46.970
I believe that rock climbing 
is the pinnacle of free climbing.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.220
I have a dream, you see.

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:51.130
What is it?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:55.870
The most difficult problem in Japan was 
first climbed and announced by my dad.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:00.260
Someday, I want to send it and be his equal.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:04.800
That's some dream.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:08.020
You must really love your dad.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:12.490
Yeah, I do.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:15.400
Wait, Master,

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.460
do you have a thing for him?

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:23.520
I guess I don't mind you becoming my mom.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:26.280
Wh-Wh-Where did that come from?!

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:31.080
I think your analytic skill 
really shines on rock faces.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.170
So, Master,

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:38.570
climb rocks and become
 a true free climber with me.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:41.680
With you?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:44.180
I promise it'll be fun, okay?

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.590
Fun...

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.070
Hey, Konomi. We're resuming practice.

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.520
O-Okay! Coming!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:55.070
Think about it, Master.

00:18:58.420 --> 00:19:00.950
You can do it this time, Konomin!

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:05.450
<i>I want to be able to climb 
just as well as these girls.</i>

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.580
I think your analytic skill
 really shines on rock faces.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.960
<i>Yeah, right! Just look at me now!</i>

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.410
Hang in there, Konomi.

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:15.280
Keep at it!

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:16.160
Konomi-san!

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:17.210
Focus!

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.870
<i>Move... Move! Please move!</i>

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:33.230
<i>I want to climb! Let me climb!</i>

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:37.900
<i>I can't do it.</i>

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:41.240
<i>God, I suck.</i>

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:44.490
I...

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:46.700
What's up?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.370
When I thought I might fall...

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:55.380
You froze up in fear, right?

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:56.700
Right.

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:00.380
Konomi-san, when you feel fear 
while outdoor bouldering,

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:05.390
it's because you aren't convinced you 
won't fall off the holds you're grabbing.

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:09.770
To overcome that fear, 
you need confidence in your body.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.510
If you have that, 
you'll be able to move freely.

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:14.600
You saw how Juzo-san climbed, didn't you?

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:19.610
With confidence, you can even 
trust your pinkie with your life.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:24.110
That is why you're training now.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:28.200
Konomi-san, work with us 
and gain confidence in yourself.

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:29.030
Yeah.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.620
Go, Konomi.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:39.130
Konomin's been super determined 
since we got back.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:43.130
She's trying to love herself, in her own way.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.890
Begin hanging leg raises.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:48.890
You can do it, Konomi!

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:52.890
<i>I see now.</i>

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:56.180
<i>I didn't know how to respond 
to Kiku-chan's words</i>

00:20:56.770 --> 00:21:00.780
<i>because I suck, can't even 
climb the Anti-Monkey,</i>

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.020
<i>and have no confidence.</i>

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:04.780
Incline sprints, go!

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:10.860
<i>Right now, I'm not keeping up with practice.</i>

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.100
You okay, Konomi?

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:18.420
<i>So, I'm going to get to that point...</i>

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:19.840
I'm fine!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.050
Good.

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:25.970
<i>Build up my body so I can compete 
together with the team...</i>

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:30.050
<i>and gain the confidence to 
speak my mind with Kiku-chan!</i>

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.200
You've got this!

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.480
Go, Konomin!

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:36.940
Just one more, Konomi-san!

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:41.860
<i>"The Anti-Monkey Rock"? 
I'm gonna destroy that thing!</i>

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:47.480
Well done, Konomi-san.

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:49.240
Amazing, Konomin!

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:52.330
Not too long ago, just some sprints 
were enough to make you faint!

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:54.950
You're making definite progress.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:21:59.210
<i>Okay, next up...</i>

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:03.100
<i>Just you wait, Anti-Monkey Rock!</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b><i>Wall 4: Powerhouse Climbers</i></b>
